			<div class="content" id="post-content-4098206">
									

<p>Lots to love here. First sentence of the SCProcedures are a decent hook, and the anomaly itself is well constructed &#8212; there's just enough detail to provide the setup, and a good mental image of the area/subject, but it moves at a brisk pace.</p>
<p>Similarly, I enjoyed the brevity of the interviews &#8212; each gives us only enough to make implicit the thing's methods and goals, and it's cryptic without coming off as if it is trying to be.</p>
<p>The only real downside to this for me is how clueless the Foundation comes off as at the end. I feel that there's far too many blatant clues pointing towards escape for them to simply neglect and ponder labelling it Neutralized. To this, I would suggest either allowing them to make the insanely obvious connections, or otherwise remove the face-smackingly loud tell of bloodied footprints in lieu of something less Goosebumbs-level spoopy as a hint that it got out.</p>

							</div>

								
					
